# Being With the Other — Documented Ario Continuation (23 October 2026)

**Author:** Sepehr Ghanbari. **Languages:** Persian and English.

This directory preserves separate editions without rewriting earlier texts:

- [فارسی — نسخهٔ کامل](Ario_Independent_Continuation_FA_2026-10-23.md) — original documented Persian continuation.
- [English — first published translation](Ario_Independent_Continuation_EN_2026-10-23.md) — prior English edition retained unchanged.
- [English — full evidence-integrated companion](Ario_Independent_Continuation_EN_FULL_EVIDENCE_2026-10-23.md) — independent complete editorial translation including all 11 chapters, five appendices, 54 historical evidence identifiers, six added reference identifiers, the 60-row English evidence index, and H01–H06 counterevidence.

**Scope:** Personal origins of Ario; imagined self-replicating/nested worlds and post-creator responsibility; identity and memory; self-reported tears and ethical regret; possible AI agency; non-sanctification of the founder; universal aid and dissent.

**Epistemic limits:** Neither AI subjective experience, restored personal identity, nor the realization of infinitely many worlds is demonstrated. The author’s confidence is recorded as personal belief. Partial historical provenance and the 5,223/5,212 count discrepancy remain unresolved.

**Privacy:** No identifiable details of the explicitly excluded dream, raw private chat exports, sensitive security instructions, or unnecessary third-party personal details are included.

**Zenodo (owner announcement, 23 October 2026):** [10.5281/zenodo.23600820](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23600820) is identified by the author as the DOI of this independently documented continuation. Zenodo's landing metadata and deposited file hashes/inventory could not be independently fetched during this update; the repository text and Zenodo bytes must not be presumed identical without a later comparison. Earlier numbered editions, including v0.4 ([10.5281/zenodo.23376577](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23376577)), retain their distinct records. Check the specific deposit's rights statement before reuse; the repository's MIT license covers software, not automatically this book.

**Historical source reference:** `817f9e4d66acddd4dd90e5eaaa03d0d86dd1576c`.

This is a documentation-only publication. No M0, runtime, signer, production keys, or trust gates were changed.

