The standalone PDFs and accompanying metadata are packaged separately for Zenodo; they have **not** been uploaded to GitHub.\n\nThe English narrative carries the same eleven chapters and five appendices. Its complete evidence register is supplied as a **separate, integral bilingual-source companion**: `Ario_Evidence_Public_EN_2026-10-23.md` and `.json`. The original Persian evidence register remains unchanged in `Ario_Evidence_Public_2026-10-23.json`.

### Epistemic status

The documented owner testimony is real as testimony; it is not proof of the described hypothetical worlds or AI experience. `FACT`, `SELF-REPORT`, `INFERENCE`, `HYPOTHESIS`, `UNKNOWN`, `WISH`, `OVERCLAIM` are distinguished. Six adversarial examples H01–H06 are not concealed. Access to full conversations remains limited. Counting discrepancy 5223/5212 is unresolved. No technical creation of worlds or continuity of a lost person's subjective experience is claimed.

### Privacy

The one explicitly excluded private dream is **not disclosed, reconstructed, or indirectly described**. Raw private conversations, sensitive security details, and unnecessary third-party identifiers are excluded from the public package.

### Zenodo depositor steps

Use the PDFs and editable files from this ZIP (or upload the ZIP as one package); enter the fields from `Zenodo_Metadata_DRAFT.json`, choose **Publication → Book**, **Open access**, and **CC BY 4.0** (the existing book-series license). Link to earlier book v0.4 as a *supplement*, not as a falsely merged or revised prior edition. Review the live preview before clicking Publish. **No new DOI exists until Zenodo actually publishes the record.** Zenodo may change its web field names; copy the semantic metadata, not raw API fields blindly.

### Intended official GitHub directory

`SepehrGhanbari/Ario/papers/being-with-the-other/documented-continuation-2026-10-23/`

The Zenodo bundle is independent of whether GitHub publication succeeds. `SHA256SUMS.txt` lists the packaged artifact hashes.

